 <article><h2>Sample-exact versus visual exports</h2><p>The atlas stores real and imaginary Float32 samples widened exactly into Float64 slots, plus derived intensity and phase. No pixels are padding. Ordinary phase.tif remains a quantized unsigned 16-bit visualization and now declares that loss in its metadata.</p><p>Applying an atlas resets the GIF spool, recordings, byte lanes, counters and derived caches. Export a full volume backup before replacing a session you need to retain.</p></article>
