 <article><h2>Field record</h2><pre id="russl-summary" class="russl-output">No staged TIFF loaded.</pre></article>
 <article><h2>Sample-exact versus visual exports</h2><p>The atlas stores real and imaginary Float32 samples widened exactly into Float64 slots, plus derived intensity and phase. No pixels are padding. Ordinary phase.tif remains a quantized unsigned 16-bit visualization and now declares that loss in its metadata.</p><p>Applying an atlas resets the GIF spool, recordings, byte lanes, counters and derived caches. Export a full volume backup before replacing a session you need to retain.</p></article>
 <article><h2>Format and execution boundary</h2><p>Bounded, finite grayscale TIFF: little/big endian, classic TIFF or small BigTIFF, uncompressed strips. Atlas imports require the exact declared placement profile and matching sample checksum. Unsupported metadata, compression or page stacking is rejected.</p><p>The corpus's language, mechanics and OME-Zarr proposals remain separate. This adapter does not execute metadata or turn TIFF pixels into independent silicon, optical hardware, or a complete RUSSL/MSSL runtime.</p></article></div></section>
