+<article><h2>Sampled preview</h2><div class="field-pair"><figure><canvas id="xpu-phase" width="64" height="64" aria-label="Checked numerical phase preview"></canvas><figcaption>PHASE</figcaption></figure><figure><canvas id="xpu-intensity" width="64" height="64" aria-label="Numerical neuron amplitude preview"></canvas><figcaption>INTENSITY</figcaption></figure></div><p>The CPU models wave phases and finite neuron evolution. GPU confirmation covers exact ring arithmetic. Saving publishes the checked Float32 field and its neuron bank together.</p><p class="fine">Neuron amplitude is a numerical coupling. Quantum, optical and physical in-DRAM operations are research models; this pipeline uses the laptop's existing CPU and available GPU.</p></article>
+<article><h2>Keep and inspect a result</h2><div class="storage-actions"><button id="xpu-refresh">Refresh saved bank</button><button id="xpu-export">Download Pixel160 TIFF</button><button id="xpu-import">Import Pixel160 TIFF…</button><button id="xpu-receipt">Download run receipt</button><input type="file" id="xpu-file" accept=".tif,.tiff,image/tiff" hidden></div><p>Each logical cell has five exact 32-bit words: residue, activation, amplitude, real field and imaginary field. A TIFF byte raster retains those 20 bytes; the five logical coordinate axes are declared in its metadata.</p><p class="fine">Up to eight prior frames are retained in the saved bank. TIFF carries one frame. Imported files are checked before Save; their old GPU status is never treated as a fresh measurement. Export a full volume backup from Virtual storage.</p></article>
