-<section id="system" class="view"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">EXECUTION BOUNDARY</div><h1>What this build actually does.</h1></div><div class="system-grid"><article><h2>Console → worker → storage</h2><p>The native console opens this application through a sealed local WebView2 mapping. Its JavaScript module worker performs the computation on the Windows host CPU. Each terminal uses a dedicated MessageChannel with bounded, sequenced binary frames. No local Node server or native terminal process is opened.</p><p>The SPIRAL shell has quoting, variables, aliases, pipelines, redirects, history, and a bounded virtual filesystem. It is not Bash, PowerShell, or a host operating system.</p></article><article><h2>Software processor model</h2><p>This specialized JavaScript field-and-byte model computes Fourier propagation, optical gates, phase retrieval, GIF spooling, and lookup-table transformations. It has no general-purpose CPU instruction set or ARM decoder and creates no physical silicon CPU. The native console and WebView2 execute on the machine's host processor.</p><p>Six table identities contain four distinct byte transformations; tables 1, 3 and 6 are identical. The deterministic byte selector produces 255 for input bytes 0–127 and 0 for 128–255. Scalar and 32-wide batched loops both run in JavaScript on CPU. Modeled steps and batches are not measured hardware clock cycles or GPU throughput.</p><p>Landauer-related values are transition-cost proxies, not measured heat. Bloch, Wigner, and penteract values are model-derived visualizations, not measurements of quantum hardware or physical five-dimensional storage.</p></article><article><h2>Data protection</h2><p>A single-writer Web Lock and transactional revision checks prevent cooperating windows from overwriting one another. Recovery validates snapshots before replacing live state. Corrupt data never triggers a factory reset.</p><p>Checksums detect accidental changes; they are not signatures or authentication. Keep exported backups. Old releases do not honor the new lock protocol and should not run on the same origin.</p></article><article><h2>Release 2.2.2</h2><p>No third-party runtime package installation. Original research attachments remain unchanged under references/. The removed cloud/auth scaffold and original generated outputs are retained in audit/legacy-scaffold.zip, not served by the app.</p><p>This embedded console uses the installed Microsoft WebView2 runtime and the included pinned SDK adapter. No Node.js runtime is required for this launch. Console 1.2.1 corrects execution descriptions; the software engine remains 2.2.2. Live worker execution and persistence remain unverified until the acceptance runner passes in a normal Windows session.</p></article></div></section>
-</main><footer><span>JA21 2.2.2 · LOCAL_BROWSER</span><span>8 terminals max · IndexedDB virtual volume · no remote execution</span></footer>
+<section id="system" class="view"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">EXECUTION BOUNDARY</div><h1>What this build actually does.</h1></div><div class="system-grid"><article><h2>Console → worker → storage</h2><p>The compiled native presenter opens this browser application through WebView2. The optional developer launcher uses a local static server. Each terminal uses a dedicated MessageChannel with bounded, sequenced binary frames. No network WebSocket or native terminal process is opened.</p><p>The SPIRAL shell has quoting, variables, aliases, pipelines, redirects, history, and a bounded virtual filesystem. It is not Bash, PowerShell, or a host operating system.</p></article><article><h2>CPU models and measured GPU confirmation</h2><p>The field simulator computes Fourier propagation, optical gate models, phase retrieval, GIF spooling, and LUT transformations in JavaScript. Legacy “GPU” byte loops remain batched CPU loops. The Semi-sili XPU tab dispatches a separate WebGPU integer kernel and records actual readback confirmation when available.</p><p>Landauer-related values are transition-cost proxies, not measured heat. Bloch, Wigner, and penteract values are model-derived visualizations, not measurements of quantum hardware or physical five-dimensional storage.</p></article><article><h2>Data protection</h2><p>A single-writer Web Lock and transactional revision checks prevent cooperating windows from overwriting one another. Recovery validates snapshots before replacing live state. Corrupt data never triggers a factory reset.</p><p>Checksums detect accidental changes; they are not signatures or authentication. Keep exported backups. Old releases do not honor the new lock protocol and should not run on the same origin.</p></article><article><h2>Release 2.3.0</h2><p><a href="/validate.html">Open the browser validation kit</a>. It uses an isolated test volume and exports CPU, GPU and persistence results.</p><p>No third-party runtime package installation. Original research attachments remain unchanged under references/. The removed cloud/auth scaffold and original generated outputs are retained in audit/legacy-scaffold.zip, not served by the app.</p><p>See AUDIT_REPORT.md, CHANGELOG.md, and the reproducible test suite in the release folder. The native console requires WebView2 and uses the existing CPU/GPU. The optional developer launcher provisions a hash-verified private Node.js runtime.</p></article></div></section>
